<article class="env-lemma" id="05NL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05NL">Lemma <span data-tag="05NL">17.17.10</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to \mathcal{F}_2 \to \mathcal{F}_1 \to \mathcal{F}_0 \to \mathcal{Q} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> be an exact complex of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. If $\mathcal{Q}$ and all $\mathcal{F}_ i$ are flat $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules, then for any $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{G}$ the complex </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to \mathcal{F}_2 \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F}_1 \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F}_0 \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{Q} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{G} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> is exact also. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/05NJ" data-tag="05NJ">17.17.8</a> by splitting the complex into short exact sequences and using Lemma <a href="/tag/05NK" data-tag="05NK">17.17.9</a> to prove inductively that $\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\mathcal{F}_{i + 1} \to \mathcal{F}_ i)$ is flat. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>